# Job: cpp — separate the two `ENOENT` meanings that `a22f8c880b` merged; restore the m6b expectations to the spec

You are a codex sub-agent under a Claude supervisor. Read `AGENTS.md` (root) §2/§3/§4.1 and `framework/AGENTS.md`. Never modify `core/**`, `bindings/**`, any `doc/spec/**`, `framework/doc/framework/**`, `doc/site/**`, other languages' trees; never lower an assertion; do not commit. Root-cause rule (user mandate): no budget/timeout increases, no retries "to be safe", no fixture changes that hide runtime behaviour; if the honest fix makes a test fail or slow, report it with evidence instead of mitigating. Do not rebuild Core or local packages. B session owns Core/bindings — if you find a Core/binding defect, STOP that item and report it with a public-API repro description. Env: cpp build dir `framework/languages/cpp/build/linux-ninja-c-e2e` (`cmake --build ... -j4`), `TMPDIR=/dev/shm/zlink-tmp-cpp`; the installed cpp binding package under `.artifacts/wsl/install/zlink-cpp` is the D-B85 one.

## Facts (`review-campaign-cpp-node.md` row `a22f8c880b`, 재수정 권고 1)
- Current Core contract (verified by the supervisor against `core/doc/spec/core/socket/07-router.ko.md:202-205` and Core `socket_request_reply_submit_api.cpp finish_dontwait_request_admission_failure`): a DONTWAIT REQUEST to a RID absent from the routing map is `ZLINK_SUBMIT_NOT_CONNECTED`+`EHOSTUNREACH` with no wait token; `NONE` mode gives `NOT_FOUND`+`ENOENT`; and `ENOENT` on a WRITABLE record is the PERMANENT terminal of an already-issued wait token whose RID was removed (`disconnect_rid`). `a22f8c880b` (written 8 minutes before Core D-B85 changed this) made `raw_binding_adapter.hpp` `transient_route_errno` treat `ENOENT` as a retryable route absence, so a permanent wait-token terminal is now retried until the deadline, and the m6b test's expected kind was changed from `unavailable` to `deadline_exceeded` to match.
- The framework error model (`framework/doc/framework/common/spec/server/00-foundation/07-framework-error-model.ko.md`, `03-spot-actor/08-routing.ko.md:322-331`): a known route that is lost = `Unavailable`; no logical target snapshot = `NotFound`; an actual reply deadline expiry = `DeadlineExceeded`. Retry exhaustion must not be redefined as DeadlineExceeded.

## What to do
1. Focused tests (unit, against the installed binding) pinning both Core outcomes as the framework observes them through `raw_route_port_t::request` (`.async()` DONTWAIT): absent RID → `NOT_CONNECTED`/`EHOSTUNREACH`, no token; issued token then `disconnect_rid` → WRITABLE terminal `ENOENT`.
2. Fix `raw_route_port` / `raw_binding_adapter.hpp` so the structured submit result and the operation phase (initial admission vs wait-token terminal) are preserved: initial `NOT_CONNECTED`/`EHOSTUNREACH` (and `ENOTCONN`/`ECONNREFUSED` if the spec lists them as transient) = transient route absence (bounded retry within the deadline, per the sender replay policy in `04-actor-model.ko.md` new bullets); wait-token terminal `ENOENT` = permanent → `Unavailable` immediately. Keep ONE owner of the classification table (the adapter), no second table.
3. Restore `test_cpp_framework_m6b_runtime.cpp` `verify_remote_bound_session_bind_classifies_retryable_outcomes` to the spec expectation (`Unavailable` for the lost/never-admitted route unless the scenario is a genuine reply-deadline expiry — decide from the scenario, cite the clause) and keep m6a `verify_bound_session_bind_permanent_absence_is_bounded` consistent (raw `timed_out` only where the deadline really expires).
4. Verify: the four touched unit binaries + `ctest -R 'm6a|m6b|channel_messaging|execution'`; if a test now fails because the behaviour was previously masked, report it honestly (do not re-mask).

